        "subject": "LU-18687 build: make lustre_compat headers transparent",
        "message": "LU-18687 build: make lustre_compat headers transparent\n\nPut include/lustre_compat ahead of the kernel headers from the\ntop-level Kbuild, which in-kernel builds do not use, and filter it\nout again for ldiskfs, which is kernel code. Have each compat header\nnamed after a kernel header pull in the real one using include_next,\nso including the native header also brings in the compat additions.\nKernel headers now reach these wrappers too, so they must not drag\nin heavy headers or need types that are not yet complete, and\nlustre_compat must define COMPAT_BUILD before its first include.\n\nExisting <lustre_compat/...> includes keep working; the following\npatches move users over a directory at a time.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: If39a50a1fd663875d51c73cd7313fccf965620e2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
